{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Mirror inventory finding F9 (`reports/stability/mirror-inventory.md`), LOW.\n\n## Problem\n\n- `src/rebar/config.py:326` `LAYER_ORDER = (\"default\", \"user\", \"project\", \"env\", \"cli\")` — canonical\n- `src/rebar/_operation_config.py:51` `_SOURCE_KINDS` — the same 5, hand-copied\n\n`_operation_config.py:128` validates a provenance label against the copy, and `config.py:337`\ndocuments that domain as \"``label`` ∈ :data:`LAYER_ORDER`\" — so the copy is asserting membership of\nthe canonical tuple while restating it.\n\n## Approach — a DEFERRED, cached derivation (a module-scope import would cycle)\n\nThe obvious fix — `_SOURCE_KINDS = frozenset(config.LAYER_ORDER)` at module scope — does NOT\nwork, and the reason is the substance of this ticket. The dependency runs the OTHER way:\n`config.py:99-101` imports `ENVELOPE_VERSION`, `OperationSnapshot` and `active_snapshot` FROM\n`rebar._operation_config`. `_operation_config` is the LEAF (its imports are stdlib only), so a\nmodule-scope `from rebar.config import LAYER_ORDER` would close the loop\nconfig -> _operation_config -> config at import time.\n\nSo derive it behind a cached accessor with a deferred import:\n\n    @functools.cache\n    def _source_kinds() -> frozenset[str]:\n        from rebar.config import LAYER_ORDER\n        return frozenset(LAYER_ORDER)\n\n`functools` is already imported here, and the deferred-import pattern is ALREADY established in\nthis module for exactly this cycle — `:199-200` does `from rebar import config as _config` inside\na function. There is one consumer (`:128`), so the constant-to-accessor change is contained.\n\nORDER is the tuple's only additional fact, and that consumer uses it purely as a membership test\n(`label not in ...`), so a frozenset loses nothing. That is worth stating rather than assuming: a\nset derivation would be wrong if any consumer depended on precedence, and none does — the only\nother reader of `LAYER_ORDER`, `_commands/show_config.py:52`, takes `list(...)` from config\ndirectly and is untouched.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] AC1: the source-kind vocabulary is derived from `config.LAYER_ORDER`, not re-listed.\n      Verified by a test asserting equality with `frozenset(config.LAYER_ORDER)` and the literal\n      being gone.\n- [x] AC1b: the derivation is DEFERRED — it does not run at import time. Verified in a clean\n      interpreter by asserting `_source_kinds.cache_info().misses == 0` immediately after\n      importing the module, then `1` after the first call and still `1` after the second, plus\n      two AST assertions: no module-scope import names `rebar.config`, and `rebar.config` IS\n      imported inside `_source_kinds`'s body.\n\n      **Corrected during implementation.** This criterion originally asked for\n      `'rebar.config' not in sys.modules` after importing `rebar._operation_config`. That\n      assertion is unsatisfiable and pins the wrong thing: `rebar/__init__.py:27` does\n      `from rebar import config`, and `_operation_config`'s own module-scope\n      `from rebar._config_coercion import ConfigError` forces the package init, so\n      `rebar.config` is in `sys.modules` on unmodified `main` too — verified by running it. It\n      would have been red before and after the change. The oracles above pin the property the\n      ticket actually cares about, and a mutation that hoists the import to module scope turns\n      them RED with the circular-import traceback.\n- [x] AC2: a layer added to `LAYER_ORDER` is accepted as a provenance label with no second edit.\n      Verified by a test that extends the compared tuple and asserts the derived set follows.\n- [x] AC3: no consumer of `_SOURCE_KINDS` relies on ordering, so the tuple -> frozenset conversion\n      is safe. Verified by a test asserting every use site treats it as a membership set.\n- [x] AC4: an unknown provenance label is still rejected. Verified by an explicit rejection test.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit -k \"operation_config or config_layer or provenance\" -q` — AC1-AC4.\n- `make lint && make typecheck`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788409067339594001,"uuid":"701f037d-fcf9-4db6-8777-be909cad0032"}